{% set local_problem %}
<p>Athens presents an interesting mix of gutter challenges. The historic homes around Athens Square and the older neighborhoods near Athens State University often have original sectional gutters that are well past their useful life. These systems leak at every seam, sag from decades of debris weight, and direct water toward foundations rather than away from them.</p>

<p>Meanwhile, Athens' newer subdivisions face different issues. Builder-grade sectional gutters installed during construction were chosen for cost, not performance. They meet minimum code but can't handle the intense storms North Alabama experiences regularly. Within a few years, seams start separating, hangers pull loose, and overflow becomes a regular problem.</p>

<p>Limestone County's soil adds another dimension. While different from the heavy red clay found elsewhere in North Alabama, Athens' soil still presents drainage challenges. Water that pools near foundations finds paths of least resistance — often into basements and crawlspaces.</p>

<p>Seamless gutters address all of these issues. No seams means no leak points. Custom fabrication means gutters sized correctly for your specific roof. The result is reliable drainage that protects your home — whether it's a century-old charmer on the Square or a brand-new build on the outskirts of town.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are exactly what they sound like: continuous gutters with no seams except at corners and downspout connections. Unlike traditional sectional gutters (made of pre-cut 10-foot sections joined together), seamless gutters are fabricated on-site from a single piece of aluminum coil — custom-cut to the exact length of each run on your home.</p>

<p>Why does this matter? Because seams are where gutters fail. Every joint in a sectional gutter system is a potential leak point, a place for debris to catch, and a weak spot that can separate over time. Seamless gutters eliminate these problems entirely.</p>

<p>We bring our portable gutter machine directly to your Athens home, feed in aluminum coil, and fabricate your gutters right in your driveway. What comes out is a precision-fit gutter system designed specifically for your roofline — not generic sections forced to fit.</p>
{% endset %}

